{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1792540000000-review-7e-docs.findings.md collab/1792530000000-engineer-7e-docs.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-Local: 2026-10-14 +07\n# Review: slice 7e documentation checked against the code (opus, read-only)\n\nCommit reviewed: `32a98db1` on `srvm-phase7e`. Diff: `git diff srvm-phase7..HEAD` over the three design docs.\nCode read: `rows.cljc` (custody-keys, check-root-custody!, task-ops, custody-baseline, pack, pack-address, lift-task*, header-custody, protect!, lift-task, check-install!, check-pendings!, check-dependencies!, accept-grant!, check-custody!, with-custody, spawn-child, restore-task, lower-task), `rows/checkpoint.cljc` (inspect-pack), `holder/export.cljc` (whole file), `holder/driver.cljc` (export-fence-step, offer-request, grant :checkpoint, source-index seam), `compose.cljc` (source-index check, holder-config-keys, driver-config), `semantic_register/layout.cljc` (lower-defect, lower-task), and `rows_checkpoint_fixtures.cljc`.\n\n## Verified true (no action)\n\n- Fork custody is nil on every row. `header-custody` with `custody-keys` gives the five-key slot by kind. A halted root takes origin only, and a header-bearing halt without origin refuses `:missing-header`. Children must be nil (`:child-header`) and are checked in the root's context (`task-ops`). These match continuation §2.5/§2.6, tuples §5.5 and UCF §7.7.4.\n- Lift order (continuation §7.1 step 10, tuples §9, UCF §7.7.4):\n  1. `lift-task*`, with `validate-frames`.\n  2. Exhaustion at `max-exact` (2^52-1) on non-halted roots.\n  3. `protect!` (`:unprotected-pending` / `:yin.k/unsatisfied`).\n  4. The slot is written.\n  5. `custody-baseline`.\n  6. `emit`.\n\n  `pack` sorts rows by `(str id)`.\n- `pack-address` is `jing/segment-key` of the wire (BLAKE3 by default), which is different from `:yin.k/root`. The baseline carries `:yin.k/root` (`inspect-pack`). The grant `:checkpoint` is compared to `pack-address` (`accept-grant!`). The offer `:yin.k/id` is the pack address.\n- Lower has three per-tree stages (`check-stores!`, `check-pendings!`, `check-dependencies!`), then `check-custody!` runs once, then `attach-streams!`. The custody table row matches `accept-grant!`'s checks and refusal statuses. `:fenced` skips `accept-grant!` (protection included), but the grammar and the `:exclusive` fork refusal still run.\n- `check-install!` checks: non-nil parent = `:yin.link/id` (`:install-link-id`); derivation `segment-key` = manifest `[:yin.module/derivations :yin.semantic/code]`; input = `:yin.module/tree`; output = `segment-key` of `(:value image)` (`:install-image`). The docs' \"self-consistency, no independent claimed-image-address check\" framing is accurate.\n- Fenced restore: every task is gated `:exporting`; waits go to `:yin.k/recovery-waits` and parked records to `:yin.k/recovery-parked`; the id counter is exact; `:yin.k/recovery-cell-ids` is set. `spawn-child` nils `:make-stream` and then restores it. Ordinary resume uses `max(local, carried)`.\n- Recovery format 2 keys exactly match `freeze`: tag, version 2, pack-address, root, pack-bytes base64, header, and state `{:gate :origins :issued :issues :children}`.\n- `rehydrate-fenced` checks the following before lower: tag/version, recovery address, inspector, root, header-agrees, valid-state. It then requires byte-identical re-encode and marks `:recovered?`. `abort` refuses `:restarted`, and custody is dissoc'd.\n- Driver order is recovery object, then pack, then the `:yin.k/fenced` journal record (`export-fence-step`). That matches tuples §7's \"after recovery format 2 and before journaling the fence\".\n- Source index is checked as a fn on `compose/open!`. It is a composition seam that `holder-config-keys` refuses. It is forwarded by `driver-config` and read by the driver. `export-version` appears nowhere in `src/`.\n- The three owner-approved UCF §7.11 edits are present:\n  - The backends are checked on a documented fragment (UCF:2902-2907).\n  - \"the canonical kernel and its two backends\" (UCF:3071).\n  - The pointer to continuation §4.6, which exists at continuation:991.\n- Cross-references resolve: continuation §2.5, §2.6, §4.1-4.4, §4.6, §5.3, §6.1, §7.1, §7.2, §10.8, §11; tuples §5.4, §5.5, §7, §8, §9; UCF §7.7.4, §7.11, §7.11.1.\n- Equal-baseline variant: the same root in another row order, while an id-counter change is `:variant-conflict`. This is stated consistently in continuation §11, tuples §7 and UCF 7.11.1 clause 10.\n\n## Findings\n\n| id | file:line | issue | correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | continuation.md:575 and :2541 (R1 row) | These still say the kernels are deleted at phase 8: \"editing both kernels' offset tables for a phase-8 deletion was not worth a slice\". That contradicts the owner ruling and §4.6. | Replace with \"editing both kernels' offset tables is outside the retained backend fragment (§4.6)\" and add the `Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)` marker/reason as elsewhere. |\n| F2 | continuation.md:715-716 | \"The fallback … lives only until phase 8.\" The register layout is a retained backend's layout, so this implies it goes away at phase 8. | Either \"remains a diagnostic extension of the retained register backend (§4.6)\", or state explicitly what changes at phase 8, if anything. |\n| F3 | continuation.md:1441-1442 | \"Until phase 8, a de Bruijn receiver refuses such a value…\" implies the refusal ends at phase 8. Since the backends are kept on the same fragment, it does not. | Drop \"Until phase 8,\" and add \"(retained after phase 8, §4.6)\". |\n| F4 | continuation.md:996-1001 (§4.6) | §4.6 names only row 4 as an exclusion the harness enforces rather than `lower-defect`. But `lower-defect` (`layout.cljc:916-948`) has just four clauses: image collision, installs, free-env value, and register payload prims. Only install rows 10-12 are refused by it before attach. The link-wait rows 7-9 and the module-context row 17 are also kept out only by the harness, and nothing in `layout/lower-task` refuses them before `rows/lower-task` attaches. Read together with UCF:2905-2906 (\"required to refuse the unsupported remainder before attach (continuation design §4.6)\"), §4.6 overstates how much of the remainder is gated. | Reword: \"Of the excluded rows, only the install rows 10-12 are refused before attach (`lower-defect` `:installs`); rows 4, 7-9 and 17 are excluded by the harness only, not by a general pre-attach fragment gate (§11 6c Q2).\" Optionally record the missing gate as an open item beside 6c Q2. |\n| F5 | UCF.md:3243-3245 (7.11.1 clause 1) | \"Fixtures … or corrupt a child task's profile\" with \"Stage: C inspector fixtures (7a)\". `rows_checkpoint_fixtures.cljc` has fixtures for version-float (`cbor/float64 3`), version-2, version-absent and no-tag, but none for a child-profile corruption. | Either drop \"or corrupt a child task's profile\" or mark it as an outstanding fixture. |\n| F6 | UCF.md:3248-3249 (clause 2) | \"extra keys (including current lease, epoch or holder)\": the fixtures cover `custody-epoch` and `custody-lease` but not holder. The code would refuse it (`:custody-key`), but the claimed fixture is absent. | Say \"(e.g. current lease or epoch)\", or add a holder fixture in a test slice. |\n| F7 | UCF.md:3506-3507 (clause 10) | \"Recovery format 2 is stored before the whole pack, both fenced before publication.\" The objects are not \"fenced\"; the fence is a journal record written after both stores. | \"Recovery format 2 is stored before the whole pack; both are stored durably before the fence is journaled and before any offer.\" |\n| F8 (low, unamended) | UCF.md:~2305 (\"The driver's exit persists recovery and body, journals the fence…\") and continuation.md:2509 (§10.6 D3 row: \"non-nil is `:yin.k/unsupported :custody`\") | Stale vocabulary next to amended text: \"body\" should be \"pack\", and the D3 row describes custody behaviour that 7a superseded. | \"persists the recovery object and the pack\"; append \"superseded by §10.8 P1\" to the D3 row's why-cell. |\n\nNothing else in the amended clauses was found false. In particular, no amended sentence claims that de Bruijn kernels are deleted at phase 8; only the unamended F1-F3 residues do.\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-14 01:45 +07\n# Task: slice 7e, documentation for phase 7 (codex writes; a non-codex reviewer checks it against the code)\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7e`, branch `srvm-phase7e` from the integration branch `srvm-phase7` (7a, 7b, 7c merged; 7d is in review on branch srvm-phase7d, its facts are in `collab/1792500000000-engineer-7d-stage-e.report.md`). DOCS ONLY: edit nothing under `src/` or `test/`. Edit ONLY: `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`, `docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`, `docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md`, `docs/orchestrator-log.md` is NOT yours (the other orchestrator owns it; put your log text in your report instead), and your report `collab/1792530000000-engineer-7e-docs.report.md`. Vocabulary per UCF 7.5.3: cursor (immutable dao.stream value), cursor cell (the carrier's box, `:yin.k/cc-<n>`), cursor-ref (the sealed ref a program holds), cell (the heap box only). Read: `collab/phase7-plan.md` (3.1-3.9 and the slice sections), `collab/7a-report.md` (D3 doc amendment list and codex 7a review `collab/7a-review.md` if present), the 7b and 7c reports, `collab/7c-review.md`, the 7d report, and READ THE CODE so every sentence is true: `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/{rows,rows/checkpoint,handoff,holder/export,holder/driver,compose}.cljc`. Owner rulings that bind the text: fork custody slot is nil; REPL custody gap accepted until phase 8; install checks (link-id = parent, image address = manifest) are enforced at lower; code and trees load through the linker's source-index, fetch and admission; A is the only code identity; the AST is never lost; BLAKE3; no compat or version dispatch (the old codec versions 0/1/2 remain only until phase 8); lease, epoch and holder never enter a body; the de Bruijn kernels are BACKENDS of the semantic-register VM with a documented fragment, kept after phase 8, not widened.\nWrite, marking each amended clause \"**Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)**\" with a one-line reason:\n(1) continuation design: sections 2.5 and 2.6 (custody slot by kind: fork nil in every row, exclusive roots carry policy/occurrence/arbitration/next-op-seq/origin, halted exclusive carry origin only; five keys only), 7.1 and 7.2 (the lift `:header`, the lower stages stores, pendings and install records, dependencies, custody once for the tree, then attach; `:fenced` mode; pack vs root id; sorted rows), 8.4 (phase 7's entry conditions met), a new 10.8 inventory of phase 7's amendments in the 10.6/10.7 style, 11 (close 6b Q3 and Q4 as implemented or as stated by the code; leave others open; record the 7a D2 ruling: root is in the baseline, so a re-emitted id-counter variant is `:variant-conflict` and the only equal-baseline encoding is the same root in another row order);\n(2) transport tuples draft: 5.5 custody table (fork = nil in every row; the slot admits only the five custody keys), 7 (pack address vs root id; rows sorted by id in `emit`), 9 (the fenced lower), 5.4 install verification as implemented;\n(3) UCF: 7.7.4 (the export-recovery object is now format 2: pack address, root, base64 pack, local header, `:yin.k/state` with gate/origins/issued/issues/children; no second snapshot body), 7.11.1 clauses 1-5 and 10 (stage letters and the inspector citation `yin.vm.ucf.rows.checkpoint`), AND the three owner-approved 7.11 edits (about lines 2886-2897 and 3050-3062 of the UCF file): say the stack and register kernels are backends checked on their documented fragment and refuse the rest before attach; replace \"the three engines intended to reconstruct canonical frames\" by \"the canonical kernel and its two backends\"; add a pointer to continuation design 4.6.\nDo not invent: if the code does something the plan did not say, state what the code does and list the discrepancy under \"design defects\" in the report. Foreground only. Report: 15-line plain summary, edits by file and section, discrepancies between the plan and the code, open questions, the orchestrator-log text (10 lines) for the owner to paste. End READY.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
