A; the harness scopes `kernel-space` to the vectors a world projected | codex F2: `(fn [x] x)` and `(fn [y] y)` have distinct A, one R and one H; both kernels dedupe attaches by checksum; editing their offset tables for a phase-8 deletion was not worth a slice |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2542:| A1 | §4.1 | the public API as landed: `segment`, `space`, `lift-state`, `lower-state`, `canonical-task`, `kernel-task`, `lower-defect`, `lift-task`, `lower-task` and the rest; `lift-act`/`lift-tail`/`lower-act`/`lower-tail` superseded | engineer deviation 1, accepted by codex: one dispatching entry per direction |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2543:| R5 | §4.2, §8.3 item 12 | the unique-preimage rule for `virt`: live-out* first, else the sole named preimage for validation only, else `:yin.k/non-portable :register-layout`; item 12 permits that refusal for an ambiguous tamper | engineer deviation 7, codex D3 and M9 (take the first preimage survived) |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2546:| D2 | §4.3 | the retained-FFI response-pair seam specified as slice 6c-post-D2, gated by the owner, not a prerequisite of 6c; `unlowerable` empties and the counts rise to 366/96 when it lands | engineer D2, codex probe 3: the kernels' re-park names their own call pair; a kernel edit outside the retained backend fragment (§4.6); **Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)**, reason: owner retains backends |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2548:| R2 | §5.3, §5.6 item 8, §8.3 items 10-11 | the native lanes run the shared fragment: 61 law-4 cases over three lanes, 350 law-5 transfers (92/16 in the quick tier); tail acceptance rows 6 and 20 on the native lanes; the reference lane keeps 89/534 | engineer deviations 3-4, codex F3; link and install rows need 2-3 days of code outside the retained backend fragment (§4.6); ACCEPTED by the owner on 2026-10-13 (6c Q1); **Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)**, reason: retained backend fragment |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2552:| L2 | §7.2 | the lower is decode, `lower-defect` (collision, installs, free-env procedure, register primitives, in that order, before any attach), `rows/lower-task` into a scratch machine, `kernel-task`; the audit allowlist entries | engineer deviation 2; codex M8; the audit's precedent of `restore-task` |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2553:| T1 | §8.3 items 14-17 | the fix round's tests named as acceptance | R1, R3, R4, F6, the audit |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2572:| P8 | §4.6, §5.3; UCF §7.11 | canonical kernel and retained backends, documented fragment | owner ruling: kept after phase 8, not widened |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2668:  **Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)** — Reason: the owner retains the backends after phase 8 on the same fragment.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2669:  The canonical lane keeps the full matrix; the retained backends keep\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2673:- **6c Q2, the retained-FFI seam (kernel edit, own slice). Open.** Land\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:190:which leaves at `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §10 phase 8. The row\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:390:**historical**: that machine leaves at the frozen design's §10 phase 8,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:651:stack-shaped machine, which leaves at that design's phase 8.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:715:install child were implemented in M4 (S3 ships r8-r11, the install child\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2907:  after phase 8 without widening the fragment;\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:3224:matrix (7d). Direct versions 0/1/2 codec tests remain only until phase 8;\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:3342: