tion.md:2419:\"Code identity (A), safepoints,\"; delete \"versions 0-2\" references.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2432:(new).** UCF keeps clauses that describe bodies the row carrier never\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2541:| R1 | §4.1 | A stays the identity under image collision; a de Bruijn receiver refuses `:yin.k/unsupported :ambiguous-image` before attach, a de Bruijn source refuses `:yin.k/non-portable :ambiguous-image` before serving; no enumeration order selects an A; the harness scopes `kernel-space` to the vectors a world projected | codex F2: `(fn [x] x)` and `(fn [y] y)` have distinct A, one R and one H; both kernels dedupe attaches by checksum; editing their offset tables for a phase-8 deletion was not worth a slice |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:2555:| V1 | §9 | counts as asserted; no three-host record in the sources read; the limits and their shelf life | honesty |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:19:one carrier; older bodies are not read.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:131:(`:yin.k/undecodable`). Equal bodies are one row. The id is Merkle: it\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:483:holding cursor cells X and Y with equal bodies, `'b` bound to X; any rule that\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:484:looks only at the set and the bodies cannot tell X from Y, but `'b`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:911:  record, not minted; cursor-cell bodies and op-ids are carried verbatim; the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:969:deleted 2026-10-11: there are no other profile tables and no legacy\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
